        "problem": "Find $f'(x)$ if $f(x) = 2 \\csc x.$",
        "worked_solution": "Here, we just take the constant out of the derivative and use the result for the derivative of $\\csc x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{\u2032}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2csc\u2061x) \\\\  & =2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(csc\u2061x) \\\\  & =2(-csc\u2061xcot\u2061x) \\\\  & =-2csc\u2061xcot\u2061x\\end{aligned}\n$$",
